{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "006G", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-abelian-presheaves}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:37a9d69c3b98ff99f938c6c4a856866733ef6e4333aed8470d2092acd133242a", "source_text": "Abelian presheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cc2bba2ee4ee0c80534d55ef20e1bdd715d2e73bdc5ef4ea7ce2ad6c594b2573", "unit_id": "tag:006G:title"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "006G", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b100a256f32bd8bf30719080db922e04afe1bd10dddef9983c74ebd02fbf4242", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we briefly point out some features of the\ncategory of presheaves that allow one to define presheaves\nof abelian groups.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d2f93057606e4ec92101eb2bce995c2774949bc6a1c3df9ab7a18ee31ca3d929", "unit_id": "tag:006G:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "006G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\rho^U_V$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$*$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-singleton-presheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1cdca0e9d1ee81293a87507eba80769abc8124109b9098a309d730e3c95ca923", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d441dedd0f37a7d680d153a8d4c1d4070321611aa07fc6f3f30a83dc031f2e0f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space. Consider a rule <MATH_0002> that\nassociates to every open subset of <MATH_0003> a singleton set. Since every set\nhas a unique map into a singleton set, there exist unique restriction\nmaps <MATH_0004>. The resulting structure is a presheaf of sets on <MATH_0005>.\nIt is a final object in the category of presheaves of sets on <MATH_0006>, by the\nproperty of singleton sets mentioned above. Hence it is\nalso unique up to unique isomorphism. We will sometimes write <MATH_0007>\nfor this presheaf.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ca5bb4c8929223f894a66062ec49a6718f58777e54b43192c7529e113e506fbe", "unit_id": "tag:006H:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "006G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-product}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-product-presheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7238a9aa3420d37a65a86e09f1bb2385cb8215015d49bc1093e7f2d1d41f81ac", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7cd4bd8b2dc0cab72488489d44244e62da8a890ce34d39b93a33183acbf41321", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space. The category of presheaves of sets\non <MATH_0002> has products (see\nCategories, Definition <REF_0001>).\nMoreover, the set of\nsections of the product <MATH_0003>\nover an open <MATH_0004> is the product of the sets of sections of\n<MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a1cd845e40a199de9bc5f16120e2038be481d2a92bbac9efaa6853135dbd161a", "unit_id": "tag:006I:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "006G", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}(U) \\times \\mathcal{G}(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$V \\subset U \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n(\\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G})(U)\n\\longrightarrow\n(\\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G})(V)\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$(s, t) \\mapsto (s|_V, t|_V)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0010": "$p : \\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0011": "$q : \\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Mor(\\mathcal{H}, \\mathcal{F} \\times \\mathcal{G})\n= \\Mor(\\mathcal{H}, \\mathcal{F}) \\times\n\\Mor(\\mathcal{H}, \\mathcal{G})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1ecab8f2476641fe11ca065e21ed963465ea523c2e36f1086571c42d4a7bf636", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:942b7a65f25a1d3ae34fc4094abacdbc7bf6dd5bbac922d8ef1bdf1ba8a2a43c", "source_text": "Namely, suppose <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are\npresheaves of sets on the topological space <MATH_0003>.\nConsider the rule <MATH_0004>,\ndenoted <MATH_0005>. If <MATH_0006>\nare open then define the restriction mapping\n<MATH_0007>\nby mapping <MATH_0008>. Then it is immediately\nclear that <MATH_0009> is a presheaf.\nAlso, there are projection maps\n<MATH_0010>\nand\n<MATH_0011>.\nWe leave it to the reader to show that\nfor any third presheaf <MATH_0012> we have\n<MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8eeb872978d343efe0f9c7602ad76569e6547c02cc962c6dc37053e74780fe4d", "unit_id": "tag:006I:proof"}
